.TH HALO-KEYBOARD-HANDLER 8 "August 2026" "halo-keyboard 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
halo-keyboard-handler \- translate the Yoga Book Halo surface into keyboard and touchpad input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halo-keyboard-handler
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-d ]
.RB [ \-m " magnitude" ]
.RB [ \-D " duration-ms" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B halo-keyboard-handler
reads multitouch events from
.BR /dev/halo_keyboard ,
creates virtual keyboard and internal touchpad devices through uinput, and
optionally sends force-feedback effects to the Yoga Book haptic actuators.
.PP
The systemd service runs with
.B /etc/halo-keyboard
as its working directory. Configuration is read from
.BR hardware.csv ,
.BR touchpad.csv ,
and
.BR layout.csv .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Print command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-d
Enable debug logging. The option may be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-m " magnitude"
Set haptic feedback magnitude. The packaged service uses 1.0.
.TP
.BI \-D " duration-ms"
Set haptic feedback duration in milliseconds. The packaged service uses 6.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/halo-keyboard/
Hardware, touchpad, and keyboard layout configuration.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-halo-keyboard.rules
Device aliases and service activation.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/udev/hwdb.d/61-halo-keyboard.hwdb
Yoga Book device classification and calibration.
.TP
.B /dev/halo_keyboard
Stable alias for the Goodix input event device.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR udev (7),
.BR systemd-hwdb (8)
